to the chaotic scene.

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.823
JESSE: In total,
six people are killed,

00:03:10.957 --> 00:03:14.994
dozens injured, and hundreds
of lives changed forever.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.098
I followed the vehicle and
I saw everything that happened,

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:22.101
I kind of stood there
in shock for a little bit.

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:26.139
And then from there on,

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:28.607
it kind of hit me like,
I need to go find my daughter.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:33.212
When I found her,
she was in front of the vehicle.

00:03:33.345 --> 00:03:35.348
Once we got
to the fourth floor ICU,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:40.219
it was there that they told me
that they had to intubate her

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:43.489
because of the seriousness
of her injuries.

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:46.959
WOMAN 6: Oh, my God! Oh!

00:03:47.093 --> 00:03:48.962
JESSE: Authorities
immediately try to figure out

00:03:49.095 --> 00:03:53.733
who did this, but the driver
of the red SUV disappears.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:57.803
However, shortly after,
he's captured on camera

00:03:57.937 --> 00:04:00.773
running through yards
in the surrounding neighborhood.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:02.808
So what do we think
we-- that he's doing?

00:04:02.942 --> 00:04:04.510
We think he's fleeing the scene.

00:04:04.644 --> 00:04:07.313
JESSE: But as you'll see,
the unidentified man

00:04:07.446 --> 00:04:11.150
then shows up on a ring doorbell
camera at a nearby house.

00:04:12.718 --> 00:04:15.855
Hey, can I-- I called
some-- I called an Uber

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:17.490
and I'm supposed to be
waiting for it over here,

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:18.557
but I don't know
when it's coming.

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.492
Can you call it for me, please?

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:22.462
- I'm homeless.
JESSE: Police eventually

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.996
track the man down.

00:04:24.463 --> 00:04:26.432
POLICEMAN 2: Hands up!
Hands where I can see them.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.267
POLICEMAN 3: Hands up!
- Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:30.369
POLICEMAN 4: Hands up, hands up!

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:32.672
BROOKS: Wait!
POLICEMAN 4: Get on the ground!

00:04:46.118 --> 00:04:48.655
JESSE: Is Darrell Brooks
though, the driver?

00:04:55.661 --> 00:04:57.596
JESSE: After he's detained,
authorities begin

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:00.500
to question him,
including the FBI.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.740
You know that he-- during
his adult life, moved around

00:05:07.874 --> 00:05:10.443
to several different states
and had collected

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:13.813
criminal histories in all
of those places along the way.

00:05:23.155 --> 00:05:25.324
They're not obligated to tell

00:05:25.457 --> 00:05:28.394
a suspect everything.

00:05:28.527 --> 00:05:31.097
They're not obligated to tell
them the truth about everything.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.477
JESSE: This is just the start
of Brooks's interrogation.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:48.681
When we return,
things get very tense.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:08.734
It's sad that an event
that is supposed to be

00:06:08.867 --> 00:06:12.071
happy and joyous
just turned into something

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:15.875
so horrific
in a matter of just minutes.

00:06:16.008 --> 00:06:19.878
(screams)

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.882
JESSE: In November,
2021, tragedy strikes

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:26.952
the small town of Waukesha,
Wisconsin, when a rogue SUV

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:30.022
barrels down the route
of an annual Christmas parade,

00:06:30.155 --> 00:06:32.725
leaving six dead
and dozens injured.

00:06:35.995 --> 00:06:39.298
JESSE: While police located
the abandoned red Ford SUV,

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.168
they eventually apprehend
the suspected driver.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.670
Darrel Brooks Cameras
captured him going

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:47.640
from yard to yard
and even trying to seek refuge

00:06:47.773 --> 00:06:51.076
at a stranger's home while
his behavior is suspicious.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:52.545
Is he the killer?

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.652
They weren't
fully honest with him.

00:06:59.785 --> 00:07:03.222
They didn't tell him exactly
what the investigation was.

00:07:03.356 --> 00:07:04.656
In fact,
they told him this was more

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.459
about the domestic
violence incident.

00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:11.664
Investigators start by asking

00:07:11.797 --> 00:07:13.799
Brooks about an incident
with his on again,

00:07:13.932 --> 00:07:16.269
off again,
girlfriend Erica Patterson.

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:18.804
An incident
that occurred right before

00:07:18.937 --> 00:07:21.474
he allegedly drove
the car into the parade.

00:07:33.686 --> 00:07:36.788
Why Erica was here in Waukesha
in the first place?

00:07:36.922 --> 00:07:39.625
It was an attempt to get
away from Mr. Brooks after

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:43.095
he had run her over
with that same SUV

00:07:43.229 --> 00:07:45.264
in Milwaukee just
a few weeks earlier.

00:08:01.647 --> 00:08:03.482
To harass her
the way that he did,

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.785
to force her into the vehicle,

00:08:06.285 --> 00:08:07.819
to punch her in the face,

00:08:07.953 --> 00:08:10.423
a picture of Erica Patterson
and that black eye,

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:13.225
just shows just a fraction
of what she's been through.

00:08:13.359 --> 00:08:15.795
JESSE: Although Brooks
denies attacking Patterson,

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:18.897
detectives press and search
for a possible connection

00:08:19.031 --> 00:08:21.667
between the altercation
and the parade attack.

00:08:26.271 --> 00:08:26.938 line:92%
- There's no question

00:08:27.205 --> 00:08:29.641
he's enraged,
and we see it in the video

00:08:29.775 --> 00:08:31.577
when he's
with his ex-girlfriend.

00:08:31.710 --> 00:08:33.712
JESSE: And then
investigators question Brooks

00:08:33.845 --> 00:08:36.148
further
on details of his account.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.274
In the whole...

00:09:03.142 --> 00:09:06.245
story that he concocted
about getting a ride out here

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:10.683
from a friend, that was
all just intended to mislead.

00:09:24.563 --> 00:09:25.931
I think what was interesting is,

00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:27.933
they were both playing
mind games with each other.

00:09:28.066 --> 00:09:30.369
He knew this was not about
a domestic violence incident,

00:09:30.503 --> 00:09:32.671
and neither of them
are completely truthful

00:09:32.805 --> 00:09:33.839
with each other.

00:09:46.151 --> 00:09:48.620
They were persistent,
they were fair.

00:09:48.987 --> 00:09:51.123
And at the very end,
they confronted him

00:09:51.424 --> 00:09:54.727
with video
and photographic evidence.

00:10:19.718 --> 00:10:21.220
JESSE: Brooks would
end up being charged

00:10:21.353 --> 00:10:24.423
with 76 criminal counts,
including 6 counts

00:10:24.557 --> 00:10:27.159
of first degree
intentional homicide.

00:10:27.293 --> 00:10:31.530
But this is just the beginning.
The trial of Darrel Brooks Jr.

00:10:31.663 --> 00:10:34.400
is something
no one will soon forget.

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:35.734
- Furthermore...
BROOKS: Not just today.

00:10:35.868 --> 00:10:37.136
- I'm not done.
BROOKS: Cause that's a lie.

00:10:37.269 --> 00:10:38.571
JUDGE DARROW: Let him finish.
BROOKS: Cause if he...

00:10:38.704 --> 00:10:39.939
JUDGE DARROW: Let him finish.
BROOKS: If we don't open

00:10:40.072 --> 00:10:41.607
the door on that-- No,
since he wanna make a record

00:10:41.740 --> 00:10:44.509
and not be accurate, so let's
be accurate all on the record

00:10:44.643 --> 00:10:46.212
since you think
you know so much.

00:10:57.923 --> 00:11:00.759
JESSE: Almost a year
after a red SUV barreled down

00:11:00.892 --> 00:11:03.128
a parade route
in Waukesha, Wisconsin,

00:11:03.262 --> 00:11:06.198
killing six people
and injuring dozens of others,

00:11:06.332 --> 00:11:09.201
the alleged driver
of that vehicle is on trial.

00:11:09.334 --> 00:11:12.838
Darrell Brooks Jr.
faced 76 criminal counts,

00:11:12.971 --> 00:11:15.607
including
intentional homicide charges.

00:11:15.741 --> 00:11:18.210
This was an accident
and he mistakenly wandered

00:11:18.344 --> 00:11:21.046
onto the parade route.
After passing all this,

00:11:21.413 --> 00:11:22.948
all he had to do was stop.

00:11:23.181 --> 00:11:24.817
They could have
paused the parade.

00:11:25.017 --> 00:11:26.152
He didn't.

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:28.820
It was intentional.

00:11:29.087 --> 00:11:32.825
JESSE: This trial though,
was anything but conventional.

00:11:33.125 --> 00:11:36.796
Do you wish to represent
yourself in this case?

00:11:38.897 --> 00:11:39.932
BROOKS: Yes, I do.

00:11:40.065 --> 00:11:41.566
There are times
when an individual

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:45.370
chooses to represent himself
and it ignores to his benefit.

00:11:45.504 --> 00:11:47.840
There are times when
jurors can actually feel

00:11:47.973 --> 00:11:49.441
sorry for the defendant.

00:11:49.575 --> 00:11:51.176
This incident was not planned,

00:11:51.476 --> 00:11:53.112
this incident
was not intentional.

00:11:53.512 --> 00:11:56.014
A lot of suffering
involved in this incident.

00:11:56.348 --> 00:11:58.984
A lot, a lot
of misunderstanding.

00:11:59.685 --> 00:12:02.321
This trial was unlike
any other trial any of us

00:12:02.454 --> 00:12:04.556
have ever been involved in

00:12:04.689 --> 00:12:06.992
because
of his self representation.

00:12:07.158 --> 00:12:08.994
BROOKS: I would
like to represent myself,

00:12:09.128 --> 00:12:12.397
to represent myself
as a sovereign citizen.

00:12:12.698 --> 00:12:14.700
Throughout the trial,
Darrell Brooks would bring up

00:12:14.833 --> 00:12:16.234
many things
that were irrelevant.

00:12:16.368 --> 00:12:18.036
One of them was
that he was a sovereign citizen.

00:12:18.169 --> 00:12:20.138
It basically
was that he's not a citizen

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:22.741
of the United States,
and therefore the government,

00:12:22.875 --> 00:12:26.645
the judge, the law doesn't
have any control over him.

00:12:26.778 --> 00:12:29.481
We all kind
of figured he was gonna go

00:12:30.082 --> 00:12:32.651
the sovereign
citizen direction there.

00:12:32.785 --> 00:12:34.253
It was just one
of those where we're going,

00:12:34.386 --> 00:12:36.388
"oh, great, here we go.

00:12:36.521 --> 00:12:37.889
It's gonna be a rodeo."

00:12:38.023 --> 00:12:40.325
Are we gonna address
subject matter jurisdiction?

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:42.994
JUDGE DARROW: The written
decision that I previously

00:12:43.128 --> 00:12:44.896
entered is what I will stand on.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.898
I don't think
he actually really believes

00:12:47.032 --> 00:12:48.166
that he's a sovereign citizen.

00:12:48.299 --> 00:12:49.635
I don't think
he believed that there was

00:12:49.768 --> 00:12:51.336
an issue of subject
matter jurisdiction.

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:53.405
I think he's smarter than that.

00:12:53.538 --> 00:12:57.575
His motive was just
to be a disturbance.

00:12:57.709 --> 00:13:00.379
BROOKS: Objection.
Leading the witness. So to be...

00:13:00.512 --> 00:13:02.915
JUDGE DARROW: It's overruled.
Now you may answer the question.

00:13:03.048 --> 00:13:05.017
BROOKS: Grounds
for the overrule, your Honor.

00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.318
JUDGE DARROW: It's overruled.
You may answer.

00:13:06.451 --> 00:13:07.720
BROOKS: Grounds
for the overrule, your Honor.

00:13:07.853 --> 00:13:10.121
It was, distracting

00:13:10.255 --> 00:13:14.059
with all of his interruptions
and ramblings.

00:13:14.193 --> 00:13:17.562
Would you describe them all
as being about teenage years?

00:13:17.896 --> 00:13:19.098
BROOKS: Objection.

00:13:20.065 --> 00:13:21.500
JUDGE DARROW: Overruled.
He may answer.

00:13:21.633 --> 00:13:23.402
BROOKS: He's at the grounds,
your Honor.

00:13:23.535 --> 00:13:26.138
Do you even know
the State of Wisconsin?

00:13:26.271 --> 00:13:28.273
FEMALE ATTORNEY: Objection.
BROOKS: Grounds. Grounds.

00:13:28.907 --> 00:13:30.542
JUDGE DARROW: Sustained.
- He would,

00:13:31.043 --> 00:13:32.844
on the flip of a switch without,

00:13:32.978 --> 00:13:37.983
without notice,
just go off on irrelevant topics

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.051
and not let it go.

00:13:40.185 --> 00:13:41.687
The defense would like
to call the plaintiff's

00:13:41.820 --> 00:13:43.489
state of Wisconsin to stand.

00:13:43.722 --> 00:13:45.291
I object.

00:13:45.658 --> 00:13:47.092
JUDGE DARROW:
The objection is noted.

00:13:47.226 --> 00:13:49.661
It is sustained.
Call your next witness, please.

00:13:49.995 --> 00:13:51.630
BROOKS: Reasons for the sustain?

00:13:51.763 --> 00:13:52.864
JUDGE DARROW: Not relevant.

00:13:52.998 --> 00:13:54.800
I believe the jury
deserves to know

00:13:54.933 --> 00:13:56.301
who the plaintiff
is in this manner.

00:13:56.434 --> 00:13:57.869
You don't know
who the plaintiff is.

00:13:58.002 --> 00:13:59.204
JUDGE DARROW: Mr. Brooks,
please move on.

00:13:59.338 --> 00:14:00.805
JESSE: But Brooks's outbursts

00:14:00.939 --> 00:14:03.041
would become even more volatile.

00:14:03.175 --> 00:14:04.643
I'm a grown man with grown kids.

00:14:04.777 --> 00:14:07.479
Ain't nobody gonna talk
to me like that. Nobody.

00:14:07.813 --> 00:14:09.181
He reminded me
of a two year old.

00:14:09.315 --> 00:14:12.551
Every time something
started to go not his way,

00:14:12.684 --> 00:14:14.887
he would throw a temper tantrum.
Literally.

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.489
JUDGE DARROW: This court
ordered Mr. Brooks be removed

00:14:17.623 --> 00:14:21.159
from the courtroom due
to repeated interruptions.

00:14:21.293 --> 00:14:23.828
He took his shirt off as well.

00:14:23.962 --> 00:14:26.865
I'm also told
that he is threatening

00:14:26.998 --> 00:14:29.267
to throw and break items.

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:31.970
JESSE: And Judge Jennifer
Darrow would find herself

00:14:32.104 --> 00:14:34.973
on the receiving end
of much of Brooks's blowups.

00:14:35.106 --> 00:14:36.642
I don't care,
which you believed fully.

00:14:36.775 --> 00:14:38.310
- Alright.
- It's not a game.

00:14:38.443 --> 00:14:42.248
The amount of lashing out
and disrespects...

00:14:43.848 --> 00:14:45.183
was beyond belief.

00:14:45.384 --> 00:14:46.952
JUDGE DARROW: Mr. Brooks.
- Whoa, ma'am, stop.

00:14:47.085 --> 00:14:49.021
- Stop it.
- You aren't even letting me

00:14:49.154 --> 00:14:50.355
- ask the questions.
BROOKS: You're a public servant.

00:14:50.489 --> 00:14:51.724
(claps) I respect
your courtroom.

00:14:51.857 --> 00:14:54.159
I respect you.
You're a public servant, though.

00:14:54.292 --> 00:14:56.060
(claps) Your job
is to be the referee.

00:14:56.194 --> 00:14:58.429
You know, I didn't think that

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.832
he would be that disrespectful.

00:15:00.965 --> 00:15:05.104
He has no respect
for humankind at all.

00:15:05.237 --> 00:15:06.472
FEMALE ATTORNEY:
I would like to provide

00:15:06.605 --> 00:15:10.609
the defendant
and the court with a passage...

00:15:10.743 --> 00:15:12.711
BROOKS: So that had to be,
that had to be said,

00:15:12.844 --> 00:15:14.980
so it's (mocking voice)
"the defendant."

00:15:16.581 --> 00:15:17.682
JUDGE DARROW:
That's not how it was said.

00:15:17.816 --> 00:15:18.784
BROOKS:
That was how it was said.

00:15:18.917 --> 00:15:20.019
You wanna run a record back?

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.653
FEMALE ATTORNEY:
I need to take a break.

00:15:21.786 --> 00:15:24.389
This man right now is
having a stare down with me.

00:15:24.523 --> 00:15:27.159
It's very disrespectful,
he pounded his fist.

00:15:27.292 --> 00:15:29.027
Frankly, it makes me scared.

00:15:29.161 --> 00:15:32.164
But she has to listen
to that and respond to it.

00:15:32.297 --> 00:15:33.799
So her temperament was--

00:15:33.932 --> 00:15:35.800
She deserves
high praise for that.

00:15:35.934 --> 00:15:38.703
JESSE: Coming up, we break
down the legal arguments

00:15:38.837 --> 00:15:40.004
for each side.

00:15:40.138 --> 00:15:41.940
And before the final decision,

00:15:42.073 --> 00:15:44.910
the families
don't hold anything back.

00:15:45.043 --> 00:15:46.712
I can only hope
they lock you away someplace

00:15:46.845 --> 00:15:49.181
so deep the rats
chew on your fingers at night.

00:15:57.256 --> 00:15:59.057
JUDGE DARROW: Mr. Brooks's
statement that the audio

00:15:59.191 --> 00:16:02.394
doesn't work when I mute
him is simply false.

00:16:02.527 --> 00:16:04.863
BROOKS: I can't say nothing
about the audio not working,

00:16:04.996 --> 00:16:06.798
so you need to stop
lying on the record!

00:16:06.932 --> 00:16:10.235
JESSE: In 2022,
a jury in Waukesha, Wisconsin,

00:16:10.369 --> 00:16:12.870
is listening to the trial
of Darrel Brooks, Jr.,

00:16:13.004 --> 00:16:15.174
the man accused
of driving an SUV

00:16:15.307 --> 00:16:17.442
through a holiday parade
the year prior.

00:16:17.576 --> 00:16:19.911
A trial where
the defendant decided

00:16:20.044 --> 00:16:22.580
to represent himself
in wild fashion.

00:16:22.714 --> 00:16:24.782
JUDGE DARROW: You are
not being respectful

00:16:24.916 --> 00:16:26.284
to this proceeding
or to this jury.

00:16:26.418 --> 00:16:28.053
- With all respect...
JUDGE DARROW: No, it's not

00:16:28.186 --> 00:16:29.521
with all due respect,
stating that

00:16:29.655 --> 00:16:31.022
- doesn't make it respectful.
- I was giving you...

00:16:31.155 --> 00:16:33.459
JESSE: Brooks faced
76 criminal charges

00:16:33.592 --> 00:16:37.429
for allegedly killing 6 people
and injuring dozens of others.

00:16:37.563 --> 00:16:40.232
We wanted do right by these
victims and by our communities.

00:16:40.365 --> 00:16:42.300
These families
all suffered so greatly

00:16:42.433 --> 00:16:45.604
that we absolutely
wanted to do our best.

00:16:46.572 --> 00:16:49.008
I watched the body
fly up onto the hood

00:16:50.475 --> 00:16:52.911
and her head snapped back,

00:16:53.846 --> 00:16:55.280
and the body
remained on the hood

00:16:55.413 --> 00:16:57.449
as it passed
the side of my vehicle.

00:16:57.916 --> 00:17:01.453
Asking these witnesses
to relive these events

00:17:01.586 --> 00:17:03.255
was very difficult for us.

00:17:03.388 --> 00:17:05.157
FEMALE ATTORNEY: Did
you see the red SUV

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.026
strike any people in
the Catholic community group?

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:09.294
Several.

00:17:09.728 --> 00:17:13.632
It was in the air,
like bowling pins.

00:17:13.765 --> 00:17:16.902
Some of the witnesses had
indicated that they even noticed

00:17:17.035 --> 00:17:19.538
that he almost had
this look on his face,

00:17:19.671 --> 00:17:21.540
like he knew exactly
what he was doing,

00:17:21.673 --> 00:17:23.008
exactly where he was going.

00:17:23.142 --> 00:17:25.277
I saw a man

00:17:25.410 --> 00:17:27.679
focused on the group
ahead of him.

00:17:29.281 --> 00:17:31.016
FEMALE ATTORNEY: Is that Darrell
Brooks that you saw?

00:17:31.149 --> 00:17:32.850
- Yes.
JESSE: While the prosecution

00:17:32.984 --> 00:17:35.754
would present evidence
tying Brooks to the crimes,

00:17:35.887 --> 00:17:38.824
Brooks presented
another side of the story.

00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:42.160
Well, what were
the defenses to his case?

00:17:42.294 --> 00:17:44.730
First was that there was
a mechanical error with the car.

00:17:44.863 --> 00:17:48.299
We believe that there may have
been some mechanical problems.

00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:51.837
How were you able
to come to that determination?

00:17:53.205 --> 00:17:56.074
That was my initial concern
because of the noise

00:17:56.207 --> 00:17:57.609
that the engine was making.

00:17:57.742 --> 00:17:59.778
The second issue was
that they didn't

00:17:59.911 --> 00:18:01.280
have the right guy.

00:18:01.747 --> 00:18:04.316
Could you see
anybody inside the vehicle?

00:18:05.417 --> 00:18:09.454
Your answer was, "I could not
see the person real clearly."

00:18:09.588 --> 00:18:11.656
And then the last
one he brought was,

00:18:11.789 --> 00:18:15.293
the person who did this
did not intend

00:18:15.427 --> 00:18:18.763
to kill the individuals
because they honked beforehand.

00:18:18.896 --> 00:18:21.900
So you heard a horn beeping?

00:18:22.634 --> 00:18:23.569
Yes.

00:18:23.702 --> 00:18:25.370
BROOKS: Was it coming from

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:28.240
the vehicle
that you tried to stop?

00:18:28.573 --> 00:18:29.941
I believe that it was.

00:18:30.075 --> 00:18:32.110
JESSE: And at one point,
Brooks appeals

00:18:32.243 --> 00:18:35.213
to the jury's emotions,
and even improperly argued

00:18:35.347 --> 00:18:37.515
that the jury
could ignore the law.

00:18:37.649 --> 00:18:39.184
You have the power

00:18:40.252 --> 00:18:42.587
to nullify any law
that you don't agree with.

00:18:43.521 --> 00:18:46.125
FEMALE ATTORNEY: Objection.
Move to strike misstatement.

00:18:46.258 --> 00:18:49.460
JUDGE DARROW: Sustained.
JESSE: In late October, 2022,

00:18:49.594 --> 00:18:52.697
a 12 person jury reached
a unanimous verdict

00:18:52.831 --> 00:18:55.434
after about
three hours of deliberations.

00:18:55.634 --> 00:18:59.438
"We the jury find the defendant,
Darrell E. Brooks,

00:18:59.571 --> 00:19:01.974
guilty of first
degree intentional homicide."

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:05.577
JUDGE DARROW: Hey.
You are to be removed right now.

00:19:05.777 --> 00:19:07.946
JESSE: The jury found
Darrel Brooks Jr.

00:19:08.079 --> 00:19:10.882
guilty of all
76 criminal charges.

00:19:11.015 --> 00:19:12.850
We had witnesses
that identified him,

00:19:12.984 --> 00:19:14.686
we had video
that identified him.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:17.255
The fact that he was close by,
the lies he told.

00:19:17.388 --> 00:19:19.991
He darn well knew
exactly what he had done.

00:19:20.124 --> 00:19:22.861
JESSE: Nearly a year
to the day following the attack,

00:19:22.994 --> 00:19:24.462
at the sentencing hearing,

00:19:24.595 --> 00:19:26.531
Brooks faced
the victim's families

00:19:26.665 --> 00:19:29.567
and the survivors
of the parade Attack massacre.

00:19:29.701 --> 00:19:31.803
And there's, there's
nothing this court can do

00:19:31.936 --> 00:19:33.905
that would provide
justice in my eyes.

00:19:34.039 --> 00:19:37.209
So all I ask is
that you rot and you rot slow.

00:19:37.342 --> 00:19:39.410
Times where I felt
justice wouldn't be served

00:19:39.544 --> 00:19:42.113
until he had to take
that SUV to his chest

00:19:42.246 --> 00:19:44.349
exactly the same way
he treated my child.

00:19:44.483 --> 00:19:46.985
And I hope the look
on my daughter's face

00:19:47.118 --> 00:19:50.288
before you ran her over haunts
you for the rest of your life.

00:19:50.422 --> 00:19:54.326
That whole experience
really opens up your eyes

00:19:54.459 --> 00:19:59.364
to know how fast things can
be ripped away from you

00:19:59.498 --> 00:20:03.535
and can change your life
in a matter of seconds.

00:20:03.802 --> 00:20:05.270
Jocelyn is doing amazing,

00:20:05.403 --> 00:20:08.739
it's surprising how well
she has bounced back.

00:20:09.173 --> 00:20:14.146
The recovery process
has been a very long journey.

00:20:14.946 --> 00:20:17.882
Very long and exhausting.

00:20:18.282 --> 00:20:21.953
It was a lot of physical therapy
and doctor's appointments.

00:20:22.220 --> 00:20:23.888
I'm doing pretty good.

00:20:24.021 --> 00:20:26.090
JESSE: As for Brooks,
he had some words

00:20:26.224 --> 00:20:27.959
before his official sentencing.

00:20:28.292 --> 00:20:30.562
Not only am I sorry
for what happened...

00:20:33.231 --> 00:20:35.334
I'm sorry
that you could not see...

00:20:38.637 --> 00:20:40.171
what's truly in my heart.

00:20:40.304 --> 00:20:43.108
JESSE: But Judge Darrow
wasn't convinced.

00:20:43.375 --> 00:20:45.544
Frankly, Mr. Brooks,
no one is safe from you.

00:20:46.211 --> 00:20:50.748
This community can only be
safe if you are behind bars

00:20:51.115 --> 00:20:53.384
for the rest of your life.

00:20:53.685 --> 00:20:56.187
This court is
imposing a life sentence

00:20:56.320 --> 00:20:58.323
without the possibility
or eligibility

00:20:58.457 --> 00:21:02.827
for extended supervision
consecutive to one another.

00:21:02.961 --> 00:21:05.597
(audience claps)

00:21:05.730 --> 00:21:09.334
And our thoughts just stay with
our community and our families.

00:21:09.801 --> 00:21:11.736
They still need a lot of love,
a lot of support

00:21:11.869 --> 00:21:12.904
and a lot of prayers.

00:21:13.038 --> 00:21:14.305
Closure is a word that gets used

00:21:14.438 --> 00:21:15.940
a lot in this business,

00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:19.444
but I hope at least
they can rest knowing

00:21:19.577 --> 00:21:22.714
that Darrell Brooks is
sleeping in prison every night.

00:21:23.381 --> 00:21:24.950
It's really not
an understatement to say

00:21:25.083 --> 00:21:29.387
just how absolutely devastating
this case has been for so many.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:31.956
And yes, a lot of attention
focused upon Darrell Brooks

00:21:32.090 --> 00:21:34.659
and his wild behavior
during trial,

00:21:34.793 --> 00:21:37.962
but we shouldn't forget what
this case has always been about,

00:21:38.095 --> 00:21:39.630
and that is the victims.

00:21:39.764 --> 00:21:42.333
Because despite all
of Brooks's arguments,

00:21:42.467 --> 00:21:44.602
this jury seemingly
didn't believe anything

00:21:44.736 --> 00:21:47.238
he had to say,
and they delivered a verdict

00:21:47.372 --> 00:21:50.241
that holds him fully
accountable for what he did.

00:21:51.076 --> 00:21:53.511
That's all we have for you
here on
<i> Prime Crime.</i>

00:21:53.645 --> 00:21:55.513
As always,
thank you for joining us

00:21:55.647 --> 00:21:58.116
and until next time, stay safe.

